  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company is navigating a post-pandemic demand reset, with legacy PCR revenues fading amid heightened competition. Sentiment has seesawed—initial fears over market-share erosion gave way to optimism when management showcased its Co-Dx PCR platform in Europe. The core growth story now rests on fresh geographic exposure: a commercial presence in India through a joint venture that cleared 15 tests, and a Saudi-led MENA expansion. This shift from a COVID-era product line toward a broader, internationally diversified diagnostic offering is the central narrative, though commercial traction remains in its early stages.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a deliberate pivot, framing the period as one of the most strategically active in its history. The team successfully appealed a Nasdaq delisting, restoring the listing, and advanced the Kodiak PCR platform toward commercialization. Capital and organizational energy are directed at scaling the international footprint via joint ventures in India and the MENA region, while highlighting AI and a refreshed pipeline. The market views these moves as a story-building effort for a low‑priced biotech, but credibility hinges on converting early regulatory clearances and partnership announcements into sustained commercial momentum.",
